From 945c32fd68b390372c4c2d22ad688fee65ad01f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 15:57:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [AGS] Remaining rename-only sites: debug.cpp,
 agsplatformdriver.cpp, graphics_mode.cpp, main_sdl2.cpp

Per PATCH-SEQUENCE.md's remaining-rename-only-sites row -- the last item
before COMPILES, alongside the ali3dsw.cpp window-surface rewrite
(deliberately not started this session, see that patch's own row for
why). Each of these four files had its own direct, first-party bare
`#include <SDL.h>` (not a downstream consequence of another file, the
way gfxdriverfactory.cpp's failure is purely a consequence of
ali3dsw.h) -- confirmed one at a time via direct compiles.

- debug.cpp: `#include <SDL.h>` -> `<SDL3/SDL.h>`. Real changes beyond
  rename, found only by actually compiling: SDL3 inserted a new
  SDL_LOG_PRIORITY_TRACE level between INVALID and VERBOSE (absent in
  SDL2) -- this file's own SDL_priority[]/SDL_to_MT[] lookup tables and
  the config-string-to-priority CstrArr in init_debug() were all sized
  and ordered for SDL2's 7-priority layout, so every priority from
  VERBOSE onward would have read one slot off from where SDL3 actually
  reports it. Added a "trace" slot to all three, mapped to the same
  kDbgMsg_All bucket VERBOSE already used (this codebase already treats
  VERBOSE and DEBUG identically, so this isn't a new policy). Also:
  SDL_LOG_CATEGORY_RESERVED1 no longer exists in SDL3 (renumbered
  starting at RESERVED2) -- SDL_category[]'s array-size sentinel became
  SDL_LOG_CATEGORY_CUSTOM (SDL3's own "one past every predefined/
  reserved category" marker, same bounding role RESERVED1 played);
  SDL_NUM_LOG_PRIORITIES -> SDL_LOG_PRIORITY_COUNT (a plain rename);
  SDL_LogSetOutputFunction -> SDL_SetLogOutputFunction, SDL_LogSetAllPriority
  -> SDL_SetLogPriorities (both plain renames); SDL_GetKeyboardState()'s
  const bool* return type (same fix pattern as patches 0020/0023's
  system.cpp/openalsource.cpp already established).

- agsplatformdriver.cpp: `#include <SDL.h>` -> `<SDL3/SDL.h>`.
  SDL_GetDisplayUsableBounds()'s first parameter changed from a plain
  int display index (SDL2) to an opaque SDL_DisplayID (SDL3) -- the same
  "display index -> SDL_DisplayID resolution" gap patch 0015 already
  solved once for sys_main.cpp's own window-creation call sites, via a
  file-local sys_get_display_id() helper. Rather than duplicate that
  resolution logic a second time, exposed the existing helper through
  sys_main.h (dropped `static`, added the declaration) and called it
  here -- one real implementation, not two. sys_main.h needed a new
  #include <SDL3/SDL.h> of its own for this (SDL_DisplayID is a real
  Uint32 typedef, not an opaque-pointer type like the SDL_Window it
  already forward-declares, so it can't be forward-declared the same
  way).

- graphics_mode.cpp: `#include <SDL.h>` -> `<SDL3/SDL.h>`. Fixing the
  SDL include unmasked a second, completely unrelated pre-existing gap:
  `%" PRIu64` failed with "expected ')' before PRIu64" because DJGPP's
  own <inttypes.h> gates PRIu64 and friends behind __STDC_FORMAT_MACROS
  in C++ mode (confirmed by reading the header directly) and this file
  never defined that macro before including it -- this bug already
  existed, just unreachable until the SDL.h fix let the compiler get
  this far into the file. Swapped the bare C <inttypes.h> for the C++
  <cinttypes> wrapper, which libstdc++ already makes work transparently
  (confirmed by reading cinttypes directly) -- matches the pattern this
  same tree already uses correctly in
  Engine/ac/dynobj/managedobjectpool.cpp. Breadth-checked: the only two
  other files using PRIu64 without <cinttypes> (theora_player.cpp,
  flic_player.cpp) both have their own #include <inttypes.h> inside
  their own #ifndef AGS_NO_VIDEO_PLAYER guard, unreachable in this
  port's build.

- main_sdl2.cpp: `#include <SDL.h>` -> `<SDL3/SDL.h>`. No other SDL_
  symbol used in this file at all (it's just the real process
  entrypoint calling ags_entry_point()) -- rename only.

Verified: all four files compile clean individually, zero errors (a
couple of pre-existing, unrelated -Wshadow/-Wextra/-Wredundant-move
warnings in agsplatformdriver.cpp/debug.cpp, not introduced by this
patch). sys_main.cpp re-verified clean after de-static-ing
sys_get_display_id(). Full make build-ags and cmake --build ... -- -k
(keep-going) re-run: this patch's four files no longer appear anywhere
in the build's error output. Exactly one blocker family remains
anywhere in the entire tree now -- ali3dsw.cpp/.h,
gfxfilter_sdl_renderer.*, gfxfilter_aa_sdl_renderer.*, and
gfxdriverfactory.cpp (a pure downstream consumer of ali3dsw.h) -- all
already scoped as the window-surface rewrite patch, deliberately not
started this session.
